# Part 11's control arm RUNS this program (panel 226's R1, 2026-10-20): the
# strict build refuses it under `endless_recursion`, a thesis rule, and the control arm,
# `build --permissive`, gives the dropped rule the meaning the sitting's
# table pins: a function that always calls itself runs until the stack is exhausted and aborts loudly, `panic: stack exhausted`.
# The witness is the compiler-engineer's (w17-endless_recursion), one of 27 it ran before the
# resolution was written (`docs/panel/226-reports/compiler-engineer.md`).

function down(n: i64) -> i64
    return down(n - 1)  #~ endless_recursion

function main()
    print(down(3))
